      "message": "I did some digging in the arch.go and I noticed that for Darwin, we have only X86_64 in the osArchTypeMap map in arch.go. Based on our discussion, I heard that we hardcoded the arch to X86 which represents 64 bits, am I right?\n\nDo you think it\u0027s better for me to do:\n\nexpected :\u003d filepath.Join(\"host\", buildOs+\"-x86\", \"usr\", \"share\", \"bar\")\n\nor define a BuildArch and BuildTarget function in arch.go:\n\nvar BuildArch \u003d func() ArchType {\n    for arch :\u003d range archTypeMap {\n       // there are architectures that has additional suffix string (i.e. amd 64 with 4gb address space: amd64p32)\n       if strings.Contains(runtime.GOARCH, arch)) {\n          return archTypeMap[arch]\n       }\n    }\n    panic(fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported Arch: %s\", runtime.GOARCH))\n}\n\nfunc BuildTarget() string {\n    return fmt.Sprintf(\"%s-%s\", BuildOs.String(), BuildArch.String())\n}\n\nand then use it as follows:\n\nexpected :\u003d filepath.Join(\"host\", BuildTarget(), \"usr\", \"share\", \"bar\")",
